  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of the Sotas and Caballos (Jacks and Horses). Because there are only four of each rank, if you have three Sotas in your hand and someone plays two Sotas, you KNOW they are lying. Challenge them immediately.\n\nThe 'Sacrifice' Draw: If the pile is small (2-3 cards) and you have several 'junk' cards that don't match the current rank, it is sometimes better to TAKE the pile voluntarily (by intentionally lying and getting caught) to clear those cards out of the game or to gain specific ranks you need.\n\nStaring Down the Challenger: Lying in Mentiroso is as much about speed and confidence as it is about the cards. If you hesitate, you will be called. Practice playing your lies at the exact same rhythm as your truths.",
    Player: "Keep track of the Sotas and Caballos (Jacks and Horses). Because there are only four of each rank, if you have three Sotas in your hand and someone plays two Sotas, you KNOW they are lying. Challenge them immediately.\n\nThe 'Sacrifice' Draw: If the pile is small (2-3 cards) and you have several 'junk' cards that don't match the current rank, it is sometimes better to TAKE the pile voluntarily (by intentionally lying and getting caught) to clear those cards out of the game or to gain specific ranks you need.\n\nStaring Down the Challenger: Lying in Mentiroso is as much about speed and confidence as it is about the cards. If you hesitate, you will be called. Practice playing your lies at the exact same rhythm as your truths.",
